      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T15:46:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e 1. In final deps mutator to add dex2oatd dep\n\nI\u0027m surprised that we are relying on `dexpreoptToolDepsMutator`, which is meant for java libraries, not apexes.\n\nFor apexes, I think we should not call `dexpreoptDisabled` in the deps mutator at all. Instead of returning \"false\" here, we do it even more aggresively: we should add the dep for apexes whenever `dexpreopt.IsDex2oatNeeded(ctx)` returns true, just like [what we did for boot jars](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/dexpreopt_bootjars.go;l\u003d506-510;drc\u003d69e198683fc9eff07bd0f40dfda7cb87b759b5cf). This can be done by creating a final deps mutator dedicated for apexes.\n\nI don\u0027t know why `dexpreoptDisabled` is called in the dep mutator for java libraries because it hasn\u0027t been long since I took the ownership of this project, but I think for apexes let\u0027s keep things simple if we can. As long as it doesn\u0027t break builds, I\u0027m for adding the dep more aggressively.\n\n\u003e Would the errorprone concern be mitigated if we run builds on all postsubmit targets as suggested in this other comment thread?\n\nThe errorprone part is that `return false` prevents any further checks below, including what we may add in the future. Let\u0027s say one day we\u0027ve added one more check below line 231:\n\n```\nif certain condition is met {\n  return true;\n}\n```\n\nThen your `return false` will prevent that check from being executed. Running more builds won\u0027t help because my concern is about future changes.",
