      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ohh I see, I think you are right that putting this in `dexpreoptDisabled` disabled might be errorprone for future changes.\n\nOne of my concerns with creating a new final deps mutator for apexes is that it will run on every single module variant in the tree. This will likely add ~2s to the analysis time.\n\nDo you think it would be errorprone if we moved this CL\u0027s logic out of `dexpreoptDisabled` and into `dexpreoptToolDepsMutator`? e.g.\n\n```\nfunc dexpreoptToolDepsMutator(ctx android.BottomUpMutatorContext) {\n\tif apex {\n\t    dexpreopt.RegisterToolDeps(ctx)\n\t    return\n\t} # here instead of a new mutator?\n\t\n\tif d, ok :\u003d ctx.Module().(DexpreopterInterface); !ok || d.dexpreoptDisabled(ctx) || !dexpreopt.IsDex2oatNeeded(ctx) {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tdexpreopt.RegisterToolDeps(ctx)\n}\n```",
