      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T01:02:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think adding an explicit libraryName is important when invoking `java.dexpreopt` from the top-level prebuilt apex. e.g. at ToT the ctx of `prebuilt_com.google.android.adservices` will be running the following dexpreopt cmds\n- dexprept(ctx, \u003cdeapxed_services-adservices.dex.jar\u003e)\n- dexpreopt(ctx, \u003cdeapxed_services-sdksandbbox.dex.jar\u003e)\n\nIf we use the implicit naming, the module name used for `dexpreopt.GenerateDexpreoptRule` would both be `com.google.android.adservices`. The module name passed to `dexpreopt.GenerateDexpreoptRule` is important because we use it to do some [special handling for apex system server jars](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/build/soong/+/a62e65010a74fe9d460009eb6013d9cce682ffd5:dexpreopt/dexpreopt.go;l\u003d263-291;drc\u003db2fd4ff43fbb569d591ab48accc4e8765e46a529;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0)",
